0 0 0 0 7 7 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 0 7 7 0 0\n0 3 0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0\n0 0 3 0 0 3 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 3 0 0 0 0 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    import numpy as np\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    rows, cols = g.shape\n    result = g.copy()\n    \n    colors = set(g.flatten()) - {0}\n    \n    for color in colors:\n        points = list(zip(*np.where(g == color)))\n        # Find the 2x2 block (bottom of triangle)\n        # Then fill between the diagonal lines\n        for r, c in points:\n            result[r][c] = color\n        \n        # For each row that has this color, fill between the leftmost and rightmost occurrence\n        for r in range(rows):\n            positions = [c for c in range(cols) if g[r][c] == color]\n            if len(positions) >= 2:\n                for c in range(min(positions), max(positions) + 1):\n                    result[r][c] = color\n    \n    return result.tolist()",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    import numpy as np\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    rows, cols = g.shape\n    result = g.copy()\n    \n    colors = set(g.flatten()) - {0}\n    \n    for color in colors:\n        points = list(zip(*np.where(g == color)))\n        # Find the 2x2 block (bottom of triangle)\n        # Then fill between the diagonal lines\n        for r, c in points:\n            result[r][c] = color\n        \n        # For each row that has this color, fill between the leftmost and rightmost occurrence\n        for r in range(rows):\n            positions = [c for c in range(cols) if g[r][c] == color]\n            if len(positions) >= 2:\n                for c in range(min(positions), max(positions) + 1):\n                    result[r][c] = color\n    \n    return result.tolist()",
